[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（英音）]
[ti:Always Young]
[00:13.63]Why doesn't Aunt Jennifer tell anyone how old she is?
[00:21.80]My aunt Jennifer is an actress.
[00:25.66]She must be at least thirty-five years old.
[00:32.14]In spite of this,
[00:34.27]she often appears on the stage as a young girl.
[00:39.48]Jennifer will have to take part in a new play soon.
[00:43.74]This time, she will be a girl of seventeen.
[00:48.25]In the play, she must appear in a bright red dress and long black stockings.
[00:56.00]Last year in another play,
[00:58.60]she had to wear short socks and a bright, orange-coloured dress.
[01:05.30]If anyone ever asks her how old she is,
[01:09.21]she always answers, 'Darling, it must be terrible to be grown up!'
